JWasm: -Zj uses a macro before its definition, as MASM 5 does

MASM 5 reports most errors in pass two only. A line that starts with a
name not yet defined, such as a macro used before the MACRO that
defines it, is no error in pass one, and in pass two the macro defined in
pass one is expanded. JWasm reports a syntax error in pass one. Under
-Zj, in pass one, such a line is skipped; pass two reports it if the name
is still not defined.

Needed for TREE's and the GRAFTABL, LABEL, DISKCOMP, FASTOPEN, NLSFUNC
and ASSIGN parsers' HEADER, defined after its first use, and ASSIGN's
BREAK, which CURDIR.INC uses before ASSGMAIN.ASM defines it.

diff --git a/src/parser.c b/src/parser.c
index b9aab25..eccb51e 100644
--- a/src/parser.c
+++ b/src/parser.c
@@ -3225,6 +3225,15 @@ ret_code ParseLine( struct asm_tok tokenarray[] )
         } /* end switch (tokenarray[i].token) */
         if ( i && tokenarray[i-1].token == T_ID )
             i--;
+        /* -Zj: MASM 5 reports such errors in pass two only, so a macro may
+         * be used before its definition (TREE's HEADER, ASSIGN's BREAK):
+         * in pass one the line is skipped, and in pass two the macro
+         * defined in pass one is expanded. */
+        if ( Options.masm5_compat && Parse_Pass == PASS_1 && tokenarray[i].token == T_ID ) {
+            sym = SymSearch( tokenarray[i].string_ptr );
+            if ( sym == NULL || sym->state == SYM_UNDEFINED )
+                return( NOT_ERROR );
+        }
         DebugMsg(("ParseLine: unexpected token=%u, i=%u, string=%s\n", tokenarray[i].token, i, tokenarray[i].string_ptr));
         return( EmitErr( SYNTAX_ERROR_EX, tokenarray[i].string_ptr ) );
     }
